     1	# Generalization campaign: three-dataset response assessment of the frozen pipeline
     2	
     3	Branch `generalization/campaign-1` · frozen baseline tag `frozen-2026-08-01` ·
     4	deadline AAS 249 regular abstract Wed 2026-09-30.
     5	
     6	## Claim under test
     7	
     8	The 2026-08-01 ZTF white-dwarf run showed the variance census and the blind
     9	Lomb-Scargle search have complementary selection functions — but on 19
    10	truth-labeled stars, with a known mechanism, and injections conditioned on two
    11	light curves. Red-team verdict: NO-GO as a discovery claim. The flip condition:
    12	run the *frozen* pipeline on externally labeled samples large enough to
    13	measure class-specific response rates with uncertainty.
    14	
    15	G1 review (sol ×3, 2026-08-28) sharpened what this campaign can honestly
    16	claim — THREE SEPARATE response assessments, never pooled into one
    17	"selection function":
    18	- D1: the anchor (19 labeled WDs + 928-star catalog, published);
    19	- D2: conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the frozen search stage
    20	  (TESS-truth signals in real ZTF windows) — labeled as such, NOT real-sky
    21	  completeness and NOT an independently labeled sample;
    22	- D3: externally labeled, magnitude-restricted validation on real ZTF
    23	  photometry (detection completeness, frequency recovery, negative-class
    24	  trigger rate).
    25	Banned phrases (G1): "quantified selection-function measurement", "real-sky
    26	completeness" (for D2), "D3 FPR", unqualified "purity". Estimand names in
    27	METRICS_SPEC.md are binding.
    28	
    29	## Frozen-core / adapter-shell architecture
    30	
    31	- Tag `frozen-2026-08-01` = branch point. Zero edits to any script that
    32	  produced the published bundle; the referee check is an empty
    33	  `git diff frozen-2026-08-01 -- scripts/<frozen five>`.
    34	- Frozen five: `run_catalog_lomb_scargle.py`, `run_lomb_scargle.py`,
    35	  `lomb_scargle_common.py`, `build_catalog_panels.py`,
    36	  `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py`. SHA-256 pinned in
    37	  `scripts/generalization/frozen_api.py`; `assert_frozen()` runs at import and
    38	  at the top of every campaign script.
    39	- Campaign code lives in `scripts/generalization/` and imports the frozen
    40	  callables only through `frozen_api`. The frozen CLI never runs on campaign
    41	  data (its `main()` merges the WD roster and rewrites the published table);
    42	  `verify_cli_identity.py` proves the import path is byte-identical to the
    43	  CLI's internal call path.
    44	- Known frozen quirks are pinned by `tests/test_frozen_constants.py`, fixed by
    45	  nothing: the `>= 2.5` vs `> 2.5` census inconsistency (provably
    46	  non-affecting: 0 of 5,568 published ratios within 1e-4 of 2.5; campaign
    47	  metrics use `>=` and assert no campaign ratio equals 2.5 exactly), the
    48	  bootstrap's `int(source_id[-9:])` seed (harmless for 19-digit numeric
    49	  campaign ids by construction), duplicated pass-bound literals (AST-scan
    50	  test).
    51	
    52	### Campaign source_id convention
    53	
    54	19-digit numeric strings: `90…` D3 targets, `92…` D2 arm B, `93…` D2 arm A,
    55	`94…` D2 Gaussian nulls, `95…` D2 paired real-window controls. No collision
    56	with Gaia DR3 ids; always valid for the frozen seed convention.
    57	
    58	### Replay gate (blocks everything)
    59	
    60	`replay_gate.py` re-runs the frozen `analyze_star` through `frozen_api` on 25
    61	published stars (all 7 schema-v2 + 18 stride-sampled schema-v1) and
    62	byte-compares against the committed bundle. Comparison tiers: raw-identical;
    63	identical after CRLF→LF normalization (git stored the bundle normalized);
    64	identical after the documented v1→v2 schema transform — 921/928 published
    65	files were written before commit `fa16d7f` (parent `e917bd1`), which added
    66	sparse-input early-exit branches plus the `available`/`unavailable_reason`
    67	keys and bumped `schema_version` 1→2. For any star that yields candidates,
    68	the numeric path is unchanged (the new branches fire only on sparse inputs
    69	that previously crashed; all 7 v2 records exercise exactly those branches).
    70	The downgrade transform removes only the two added keys and byte-compares
    71	everything retained. Gate passes only with a nonempty roster, zero
    72	mismatches AND at least one schema-v2 star reproducing with no transform
    73	(unconditional). VERDICT 2026-08-28 (jacks-7i-5090, production venv):
    74	PASS — 7 identical_newline + 18 identical_v1_schema, 25/25.
    75	Campaign L-S runs are valid only on machine+env pairs that passed the gate;
    76	`run_generalization_ls.py` refuses to start without a matching PASS
    77	attestation (full env fingerprint + frozen SHAs + gate identity). Full
    78	928-star baseline replay running on the production machine (launched
    79	2026-08-28). Panel-stage golden gate (`panel_golden_gate.py`): PASS on both
    80	machines 2026-08-28 — science columns byte-identical vs the published
    81	exposure panel; bjd_tdb ≤ 1 ulp (~40 µs) on ~2.5% of rows (the barycentric
    82	chain sits at rounding boundaries; ns-level IERS-state drift since build
    83	time flips the last bit — measured on the production machine itself);
    84	campaign builds pin IERS via astropy-iers-data with auto_download off.
    85	
    86	### Environment
    87	
    88	The published run's venv (laptop `jacks-7i-5090`) is recorded in
    89	`generalization/env/FROZEN_ENV.md`; the numerics-bearing subset is pinned in
    90	`requirements-frozen.txt` (Python 3.12.12, numpy 2.3.x, scipy 1.16.3, astropy
    91	8.0.1, iers-data 0.2026.7.27, pyerfa 2.0.1.5, pandas 2.3.3). Discrepancy on
    92	record: pip metadata said numpy 2.3.3 but the venv imports 2.3.5; the replay
    93	gate PASSED under 2.3.5 (2026-08-28), making 2.3.5 the pinned authority.
    94	Every campaign-run manifest records `env_versions()` (incl. BLAS vendor and
    95	thread env vars) at runtime.
    96	
    97	## D1 — ZTF white dwarfs (anchor, done)
    98	
    99	The published 2026-08-01 bundle: 19-star truth roster + 928-star catalog.
   100	No re-run; campaign metrics re-read the published per-star JSONs.
   101	
   102	## D3 — ZTF × Kepler delta Scuti (real ZTF light curves, external labels)
   103	
   104	- Labels: Murphy+2019 (VizieR J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1, 14,330 Kepler A/F
   105	  stars; `dSct` flag 0/1/2 — ships its own labeled negative class).
   106	- Amplitude axis: Mo+2026 (J/A+A/710/A245): table2 = 259,883 extracted
   107	  frequencies (SNR>8) for 1,838 delta Scutis → per-star dominant amplitude
   108	  (ppt × 1.0857 → mmag); table1 = confirmed super-Nyquist modes → the
   109	  sub-hour stratum (any confirmed SNF ⇒ real mode above Kepler LC Nyquist
   110	  283.2 µHz ⇒ P < 59 min). This replaces the originally scouted Bowman+2016
   111	  join: Bowman's VizieR table carries no amplitudes; Mo+2026 supersedes it
   112	  (and is itself the published Murphy×Bowman merge, 1,838 stars).
   113	- Roster (`build_d3_roster.py`, rebuilt 2026-08-28 post-G1): gmag ≥ 13.2
   114	  (Murphy/KIC g magnitude — the named saturation proxy), ALL 610 dSct=1
   115	  survivors + ALL 76 dSct=2 (own class, excluded from headline numbers) +
   116	  2,314 dSct=0 negatives as a frozen-seed (20260828) simple random sample
   117	  (inclusion probability exactly 2314/7292, weight exactly 7292/2314;
   118	  sampling_weight column carried into every weighted estimate) = 3,000.
   119	  Before any campaign L-S run, the realized crossmatch mapping and an
   120	  ambiguity-adjudication file are committed (crossmatch frozen as DATA,
   121	  not just procedure). Amplitude coverage of positives:
   122	  456/610 with dominant amplitude; 48 > 10 mmag; 254 in 1–10; 154 < 1;
   123	  290 sub-hour; median 1.77 mmag. The 1–10 mmag log ladder and the
   124	  sub-threshold majority make the completeness turn-on curve the headline
   125	  D3 deliverable, not a defect (pre-registered: risk 2).
   126	- Acquisition: frozen `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py --roster roster_d3.csv`
   127	  verbatim (10″ cone, 1.25 s cadence, resumable); frozen QC chain via
   128	  `build_panels_generic.py` (nearest-cluster crossmatch, catflags/chi cuts,
   129	  ≥20 exp/band, BJD_TDB at Palomar — all frozen functions).
   130	- Prespecified subsets: crowding (sep < 1.0″, ≤3 objects in cone),
   131	  near-saturation (g ≤ 14.0 flagged; g > 14.0 safe subset).
   132	- Caveat on record: dSct=0 means "not a delta Scuti", not "constant" — the
   133	  D3 negative-class result is a TRIGGER RATE (never called FPR); triggered
   134	  negatives get adjudicated in W4 (plausible real variable vs unexplained).
   135	
   136	## D2 — TESS-truth transplant (DAV signals in real ZTF windows)
   137	
   138	- Truth: Romero+2022 (MNRAS 511, 1574; arXiv:2201.04158; 74 new DAVs,
   139	  TESS Cy1–3) + Romero+2025 (ApJ 984, 112; arXiv:2407.07260; 32 new DAVs,
   140	  Cy4–5). Published per-mode tables: period [s] + amplitude [ppt] + per-star
   141	  FAP(1/1000) limit + 20-s-cadence flags. 2025 revisions apply: NOV
   142	  retractions (TIC 261400271, 804835539, 317620456) and updated mode lists
   143	  for re-observed 2022 objects — latest published solution wins.
   144	- Truth model, not interpolation (`d2_truth_model.py`): for 120-s sampling,
   145	  DAV P < 240 s is super-Nyquist (Nyquist period 240 s) and the boxcar
   146	  integration response has its first null at P = 120 s — two distinct
   147	  boundaries, both making interpolated TESS photometry undefined in the DAV
   148	  range; the mode table is evaluated analytically at the template's real
   149	  `bjd_tdb`. Chain: ppt → mag (×1.0857e-3) → de-dilution OFF by default
   150	  (SPOC PDCSAP is crowding-corrected; ON = prespecified variant) →
   151	  de-integrate the TESS boxcar (signed sinc; REJECT modes with
   152	  |sinc| < 0.3, i.e. P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence, P < ~27 s at 20-s);
   153	  cadence precedence is algorithmic: cadence_s = 20 iff the star's chosen
   154	  published solution includes any "f" (20-s) sector, else 120 →
   155	  bandpass ladder A_g/A_TESS ∈ {1.4, 1.7, 2.1} × A_r/A_g ∈
   156	  {0.70, 0.80, 0.90}; the blackbody T-derivative at 11,500 K gives
   157	  (1.43, 0.80) ≈ the low rung; the ADOPTED nominal (1.7, 0.80) is the grid
   158	  midpoint covering atmosphere-model/limb-darkening uncertainty (the ladder
   159	  is non-optional — zr carries most published confirmations) →
   160	  re-integrate the ZTF 30-s boxcar analytically → compose with the FROZEN
   161	  phase protocol: one independent phase per mode; base assignment
   162	  (phase_draw = 0) seeds PCG64(TIC) and is shared across bands and across
   163	  every bandpass/de-dilution/amplitude-scale variant; the two phase-draw
   164	  sensitivity variants d ∈ {1, 2} seed PCG64(TIC·10 + d) and change ONLY
   165	  the phase vector; shared t_ref keeps the frozen two-band rule meaningful.
   166	- Windows: templates from ALL 928 stars of the published catalog (G1 fix —
   167	  the earlier 510-not-detected pool conditioned on the pipeline's own
   168	  outcome), matched by median zg mag (|Δg| ≤ 0.25, widened when thin;
   169	  flagged), K=3 per target at 10/50/90th percentile of exposures-per-night
   170	  (75% of zg nights are single-exposure; per-night median subtraction
   171	  annihilates 53% of zg data — pre-registered, stratified: risk 3).
   172	  Template matching is a TOTAL deterministic algorithm (zero analyst
   173	  discretion): candidate pool = stars with |median_zg − target_G| ≤ 0.25;
   174	  if fewer than 3, the pool widens once to ≤ 0.5; if still fewer than 3,
   175	  the pool is the 9 smallest |Δmag| stars, magnitude ties broken by
   176	  ascending source_id (pandas argsort is stable over the source_id-sorted
   177	  stats table); the pool is then sorted lexicographically by
   178	  (median exposures-per-night, source_id) — a total order, so no residual
   179	  ties — and picks are indices round-half-even(q·(n−1)) for
   180	  q ∈ {0.10, 0.50, 0.90} (numpy round). Match label recorded per target.
   181	  D2 primary detection is post-injection rule firing (detection-only);
   182	  strict frequency matching is the separate frequency-recovery estimand;
   183	  native variability in the pool is contextualized by PAIRED UNINJECTED
   184	  CONTROLS (95-prefix; stable ids indexed over the sorted 928 pool): one
   185	  control shard per unique arm-B template window. W2 stretch: fetch real
   186	  ZTF light curves at the 103 Romero positions; usable self-windows form a
   187	  SEPARATE DIAGNOSTIC arm — they do not replace or enter the nominal K=3
   188	  aggregate.
   189	- Arms: B primary (signal + real ZTF mags, real magerr), A diagnostic for
   190	  positive injections; arm-A ZERO-AMPLITUDE NULLS are the campaign's sole
   191	  confirmatory endpoint (P5, METRICS_SPEC). Gaussian-null false-alarm rate
   192	  (`FPR_Gaussian`): 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude simulations scheduled over
   193	  the 928-window frame by deterministic cycling (serial i → sorted-pool
   194	  window i mod 928, noise seed = serial); windows repeat, seeds do not.
   195	  Verification arm: ~20 SPOC light curves prewhitened to confirm published
   196	  solutions; everything else needs metadata only.
   197	- Run matrix (22 workers ≈ 84 runs/h). Core scheduled total ≤ 2,957 ≈
   198	  1.5 d: arm B nominal (1.7/0.80) 103×3 = 309; arm A nominal 309; Gaussian
   199	  nulls 1,000; paired controls ≤ 309 (unique arm-B windows); ladder
   200	  sensitivity MEDIAN-WINDOW-CONDITIONED: 8 non-nominal (R_g, R_rg) points
   201	  × 103 × 1 = 824; phase-draw sensitivity 2 × 103 = 206 (median window,
   202	  arm B nominal). Stretch additions listed separately: amplitude-
   203	  stationarity axis (scale × {0.7, 1.3}, median window, arm B nominal,
   204	  +206 — DAV amplitudes are nonstationary between the TESS and ZTF
   205	  epochs); Romero self-window diagnostic (count set by crossmatch yield);
   206	  de-dilution variant only for the SPOC verification-arm stars (CROWDSAP
   207	  comes with the ~20 downloads). Every sensitivity contrast uses the
   208	  common-subset rule (METRICS_SPEC).
   209	- Truth-model corrections found at implementation (2026-08-28): |sinc| ≥ 0.3
   210	  rejection corresponds to P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence (the earlier "197 s"
   211	  was the |sinc| = 0.5 point); D2 min published period is 115.9 s and 49/103
   212	  stars carry 20-s solutions, so few modes are affected. Phase protocol is
   213	  frozen above (per-mode independent; PCG64(TIC) base; PCG64(TIC·10+d)
   214	  for the two phase-draw variants). Blackbody derivative at 11,500 K gives
   215	  (1.43, 0.80) ≈ the 1.4/0.80 low rung; upper rungs cover
   216	  atmosphere-model/limb-darkening uncertainty; 1.7 is the adopted midpoint.
