     8	
     9	## Estimand vocabulary (names are binding)
    10	
    11	Three separate response assessments; never pooled.
    12	
    13	- **detection completeness** — P(rule fires | labeled positive), reported for
    14	  BOTH denominators: `eligible_roster` (missing/unusable light curves count
    15	  as non-detections) and `usable_lightcurve` (frozen QC passed, both passes
    16	  complete). D1 denominators: the 13 paper-variable stars of the published
    17	  19-star master table (the 928-star catalog is NOT a labeled-positive
    18	  completeness denominator). D3: the 610 dSct=1 survivors. D2: injection
    19	  targets — always labeled *conditional injection-recovery efficiency of the
    20	  search stage*; D2 primary detection = post-injection rule firing
    21	  (detection-only); strict frequency matching is the separate
    22	  frequency-recovery estimand; paired controls contextualize native triggers.
    23	- **frequency-recovery completeness** — P(rule fires AND
    24	  best_candidate_matches_dominant | labeled positive AND freq-scorable AND
    25	  S_p = 1). Freq-scorable: D3 = Mo-joined with >=1 frequency and a defined
    26	  dominant amplitude (assert count == 456; "Mo-join-conditioned" label
    27	  mandatory; joined-vs-unjoined covariate table mandatory); D2 = >=1
    28	  RETAINED injected mode (from injected_modes.csv, post |sinc|>=0.3
    29	  rejection — never the original mode table); D1 = diagnostic only
    30	  (non-contemporaneous literature frequencies; see below).
    31	  S_p (per pass p): >=1 truth frequency inside pass p's search bounds
    32	  (low: [2/baseline, 48] / d; high: [24, 1440] / d); S_best = S_low OR
    33	  S_high. Known consequence stated up front: only ~10/456 D3 dominant
    34	  frequencies lie >= 24 / d, so D3 high-pass frequency recovery is a
    35	  near-empty cell and is reported as counts.
    36	  Mo-join MNAR limitation (binding statement): Mo inclusion required
    37	  SNR > 8 in Kepler photometry and is plausibly related to amplitude,
    38	  magnitude, and mode complexity; missingness for the 154 unjoined
    39	  positives is treated as informative — the frequency-recovery curve is
    40	  therefore a Mo-join-conditioned estimand, the joined-vs-unjoined
    41	  covariate table is mandatory, and DETECTION surfaces retain all 610
    42	  positives with the unjoined stars in an explicit `amp_unknown` bin so
    43	  their detection behavior is visible beside the joined sample.
    44	  The missed-vs-wrong-frequency decomposition uses matching denominators
    45	  only: P(D AND M | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1) vs P(D | Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    46	- **correct-frequency fraction among detected positives** —
    47	  P(best_candidate_matches_dominant | rule-1 fired, Y=1, F=1, S_p=1).
    48	  Never called purity.
    49	- **frame-specific label PPV (D3 only)** — among triggered roster members of
    50	  the weighted frame {dSct=1 census positives, dSct=0 SRS negatives; dSct=2
    51	  EXCLUDED, reported separately}: weighted fraction labeled dSct=1.
    52	  Interval: FPC-rescaled survey bootstrap (B=2000, frozen seed): the 2,314
    53	  negatives are resampled with replacement, positives held fixed (census),
    54	  and bootstrap deviations are rescaled by sqrt(1 − f) with sampling
    55	  fraction f = 2314/7292 (SRSWOR finite-population correction).
    56	  No transfer to other prevalences. Output: ppv.csv.
    57	- **negative-class trigger rate (D3)** — P(rule fires | dSct=0). Weights are
    58	  constant within the class and cancel: plain Wilson on the 2,314 sampled
    59	  negatives (no FPC — conservative). Triggered negatives adjudicated in W4
    60	  (plausible real variable vs unexplained), reported descriptively.
    61	- **Gaussian-null false-alarm rate (FPR_Gaussian, D2)** — P(confirmed |
    62	  arm-A zero-amplitude null), n = 1000; window allocation frozen as
    63	  deterministic cycling of the sorted 928-window pool (serial i -> window
    64	  i mod 928), noise seed = serial. Interval: EXACT one-sided
    65	  Clopper-Pearson upper bound at the OBSERVED event count x
    66	  (U = Beta_{0.95}(x+1, n-x)); acceptance criterion (confirmatory):
    67	  U_95(x, 1000) <= 0.005. Windows repeat; inference is conditional on the
    68	  frozen window set. FP frequency-distribution/alias audit descriptive only
    69	  below 10 events.
    70	- **native trigger rate of the template pool (D2)** — P(confirmed | paired
    71	  uninjected control window, 95-prefix). Context, not an FPR.
    72	
    73	Exact D3 sampling constants (binding): negatives inclusion probability
    74	2314/7292 (= 0.31733406...), sampling weight 7292/2314 (= 3.15125324...);
    75	never derived from rounded values.
    76	
    77	## D1 specifics
    78	
    79	Labels from the published master table (19 usable stars: 13 paper-variable,
    80	5 paper-constant, 1 transit control excluded from both classes — it is the
    81	frozen pipeline's eclipsing sanity object). D1 truth frequencies are
    82	non-contemporaneous single-epoch literature tabulations of multi-mode
    83	pulsators (observed lit-vs-ZTF offsets reach 0.6%): frequency-recovery for
    84	D1 is DIAGNOSTIC only; the D1 estimand is detection completeness.
    85	Match tolerance adds a truth-quantum term: D1 +0.0025 / d (2-decimal
    86	tables); D2/D3 +0. Validation on record (2026-08-28): the engine reproduces
    87	all five published D1 numbers (11/13 L-S, 9/13 census, 13/13 union,
    88	0 confirmed + 1 candidate among the 5 constants).
    89	
    90	## Frequency-match taxonomy (evaluate everything, then classify)
    91	
    92	Tolerance: 1.5 / baseline_days + truth-quantum. f_sid = 1.00273790935 / d
    93	(frozen, the pipeline's constant). For each detected candidate, evaluate ALL
    94	(truth mode, relation) hits across the star's full truth list:
    95	  direct       |f_cand - f_t| <= tol
    96	  harmonic     |f_cand - 2 f_t| <= tol or |f_cand - f_t/2| <= tol
    97	  window_alias |f_cand - |f_t +/- k f_sid|| <= tol, k = 1, 2
    98	Classification: no hits -> `unmatched`; hits in exactly one relation class ->
    99	that class (several DIRECT hits on different modes remain `direct`); hits in
   100	more than one relation class -> `ambiguous` (excluded from strict recovery).
   101	Named estimator columns encode both axes:
   102	`best_candidate_matches_dominant` (headline; D3 dominant Mo mode / D2
   103	largest-amplitude retained injected mode; D1 diagnostic) and
   104	`best_candidate_matches_any_mode` (secondary), plus
   105	`any_top_peak_matches_any_mode` (diagnostic over the 15 stored peaks).
   106	Chance-match calibration: truth lists permuted across stars (frozen seed
   107	20260829, 100 permutations) -> accidental direct-match rate beside every
   108	frequency-recovery table.
   109	
   110	## Detection rules and the preregistered primary family
   111	
   112	Rules (all four always reported): 1 `confirmed`, 2 `confirmed|candidate`,
   113	3 `census` (any of six frozen ratios >= 2.5), 4 `either` (1 OR 3).
   114	PRIMARY endpoints — complete tuples; everything else is pointwise
   115	descriptive sensitivity:
   116	  P1 D3 detection completeness: {D3, dSct=1 (610), eligible_roster, rule 1,
   117	     best pass, unweighted, Wilson 95%}.
   118	  P2 D3 frequency recovery: {D3, Mo-joined S_best=1 subset, usable, rule 1 +
   119	     best_candidate_matches_dominant, Wilson 95%, beside chance-match rate}.
   120	  P3 D3 negative-class trigger rate: {D3, dSct=0 (2314), rule 1, best pass,
   121	     plain Wilson}.
   122	  P4 D2 conditional injection-recovery, algebraically:
   123	     p-hat = (1/103) Σ_t (1/|K_t|) Σ_{k in K_t} y_{t,k}, where y_{t,k} = 1
   124	     iff rule 1 fires (detection-only) on target t's stratum-k nominal
   125	     (1.7/0.80, de-dilution off, phase_draw 0) arm-B shard, and K_t ⊆
   126	     {0, 1, 2} is the set of strata with a usable result (missing strata
   127	     renormalize |K_t| and are flagged; the eligible-roster variant counts
   128	     a missing stratum as y = 0 with |K_t| = 3). Both variants reported.
   129	     Interval: target-cluster bootstrap 95%.
   130	  P5 FPR_Gaussian acceptance: {D2 arm A nulls, rule 1, exact one-sided CP
   131	     upper at observed x <= 0.5%} — the sole confirmatory decision.
   132	No claim direction reversal, endpoint swap, or denominator swap after the
   133	first campaign L-S run.
   134	
   135	## Units of analysis and intervals
   136	
   137	- D1/D3: the star is the unit. Wilson 95% on unweighted proportions; plain
   138	  Wilson on the negatives class (weights cancel); survey bootstrap for PPV;
   139	  ESS-Wilson only for other descriptive weighted proportions, labeled
   140	  approximate.
   141	- D2: the TESS target (TIC) is the CLUSTER; inference is CONDITIONAL on the
   142	  frozen window assignment (report unique window count and reuse table —
   143	  windows repeat across targets, and a target-only bootstrap does not
   144	  represent the 928-window frame; stated as a limitation).
   145	  Estimator: per-target mean over its replicates within a scenario/stratum;
   146	  aggregate = equal-weight mean over the 103 targets (a scenario mix, NOT
   147	  the 928-window frame). Bootstrap: resample the 103 TICs with replacement
   148	  (B = 2000, frozen seed 20260830), carrying ALL of a resampled target's
   149	  replicates, paired census/L-S outcomes, phases, and scenario results
   150	  jointly; identical resample draws across scenarios (common random
   151	  numbers). Percentile 95% intervals; if a statistic is degenerate
   152	  (all-0/all-1), report the exact one-sided CP bound at the target level
   153	  instead. Pooled exact McNemar is PROHIBITED for D2; use the target-cluster
   154	  paired-difference bootstrap.
   155	- Sensitivity contrasts (D2 ladder, phase draws, amplitude-stationarity):
   156	  COMMON-SUBSET RULE — every contrast against nominal is computed with
   157	  nominal re-evaluated on the same median-window (K=1) subset and the same
   158	  bootstrap draws. Min-max across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified
   159	  finite-grid sensitivity range", never a confidence band; endpoint
   160	  scenarios identified. De-dilution and amplitude-stationarity are separate
   161	  axes.
   162	
   163	## Complementarity (census vs L-S)
   164	
   165	Per dataset, on labeled positives with both methods available and usable:
   166	C = census flag; L = rule-1 detection (detection-only, symmetric margins).
   167	Report the full 2x2, both discordant fractions, union completeness, and
   168	incremental yields with intervals (Wilson for D1/D3; cluster bootstrap for
   169	D2). Exact McNemar secondary (D1/D3 only; marginal homogeneity, not
   170	complementarity).
   171	
   172	## Surfaces
   173	
   174	Surfaces exist for D2 and D3 only (D1 has no amplitude axis). Two
   175	endpoints, separate files: (a) rule-1 DETECTION completeness over ALL
   176	labeled positives — stars without a defined amplitude (the 154 unjoined
   177	D3 positives) fall in an explicit `amp_unknown` bin (bin index −1), so
   178	the full 610-star denominator is preserved; (b) frequency recovery over
   179	the scorable subset only. Coordinates per star (frozen): D3 = dominant Mo
   180	mode (period from dominant frequency; historical Kepler-band dominant
   181	amplitude, mmag — explicitly non-contemporaneous, not a ZTF-g threshold);
   182	D2 = largest-amplitude RETAINED injected mode (period; published TESS
   183	amplitude, ppt). Bins half-open [lo, hi); explicit underflow and overflow
   184	bins; no smoothing, no monotonic fitting, no interpolation. Edges frozen:
   185	period {100 s, 200 s, 500 s, 1000 s, 2000 s, 0.05 d, 0.2 d, 1 d, 10 d,
   186	100 d}; amplitude D3 {0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50} mmag with top bin
   187	[50, inf); D2 {0.5, 2, 5, 10, 30} ppt with top bin [30, inf);
   188	median-exposures-per-night {1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5} with top bin [5, inf).
   189	Cells below 5 stars: counts only. Amplitude axes are invariant across
   190	scenarios (never the ladder-scaled injected amplitude).
   191	
   192	## Eligibility and attrition
   193	
   194	Both denominators always reported (see detection completeness). Attrition
   195	table (roster -> fetched -> crossmatched -> QC-passed -> both-passes) by
   196	class, amplitude stratum (including `amp_unknown`), Mo-join status,
   197	magnitude, dominant period, Teff (declared the color surrogate — Murphy
   198	carries no color column and Teff is its physical equivalent), and crowding
   199	(cone object count, nearest-separation). The negative-sample balance
   200	diagnostic (sampled vs full-frame quantiles of gmag/Teff/RA/Dec) is part
   201	of the roster report (`roster_report.json`) and is a required output. D3 near-saturation strata: g <= 14.0 flagged,
   202	g > 14.0 safe (boundary in the flagged stratum). Unavailable passes never
   203	silently dropped; missing light curves enter eligible-roster estimands as
   204	non-detections.
   205	
   206	## Guards
   207	
   208	- Assert no campaign census ratio equals 2.5 exactly.
   209	- Assert every scored JSON has complete == true, both passes present.
   210	- D2 truth ONLY from injected_modes.csv; assert every scored D2 shard id
   211	  appears there (or is a null/control).
   212	- Manifest: SHA-256 of every input file, env versions, frozen + campaign
   213	  file SHAs, replay attestation reference, spec file SHA-256.
   214	
   215	## Outputs
   216	
   217	`generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/metrics/`: per_star.csv,
   218	completeness_by_class_pass_rule.csv, contingency_complementarity.json,
   219	trigger_rates.csv, ppv.csv (D3), fp_frequency_distribution.csv,
   220	chance_match.json, surfaces/*.csv, sensitivity.csv, attrition.csv,
   221	d2_cluster_completeness.csv (D2), manifest.json, inputs_sha256.json.
   222	Figures via plot_generalization.py from these CSVs only.

